            <ArticleTitle>[Endorectal &quot;Shchetkin symptom&quot; in acute surgical diseases and injuries of the abdominal organs].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of the digital rectal examination of 218 patients with &quot;acute abdomen&quot; syndrome are generalized here. 145 patients (66.5%) showed a greater pain-fullness at the detachment of the finger from the anterior wall of the rectum than at the pressing on the latter. 183 patients were operated upon; in 126 of them free liquid was found in the abdominal cavity. The endorectal &quot;Shchetkin symptom&quot; was positive in 79% of operated patients (in 93.7% of patients with abdominal free liquid found at the operation).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
